WEBVTT

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:27.520
<i>The year is 1889.</i>

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.570
<i>The fantastic submarine Nautilus
was in pursuit of an airship</i>

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:34.360
<i>carrying Gargoyle when they
fell into a trap set by him.</i>

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.240
<i>They were encircled by
a field of sea mines.</i>

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:40.030
<i>The Nautilus and her crew were saved
from a perilous situation</i>

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:44.000
<i>by the heroic actions of none other
than Jean and the Grandis gang.</i>

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:55.550
I'm opposed to such a proposal.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.300
We have a great task ahead of us.

00:01:58.890 --> 00:02:02.140
We have concentrated our total
efforts towards this objective.

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:10.100
To take on new crewmembers we know
nothing of will hinder our mission.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:13.980
Not only that, but won't it place the
Nautilus in even more danger?

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:17.200
But we are short of personnel,

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:22.870
and we mustn't forget their courage
in our battle with Gargoyle.

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:26.540
As long as they think of
Gargoyle as an enemy,

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.960
won't their goal be the same as ours?

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.750
There is one thing that bothers me.

00:02:31.750 --> 00:02:37.800
They might take the secrets of the
Nautilus back, and misuse them.

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:40.300
I don't think that should worry us.

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:44.470
The theories behind our science could
never be understood by them.

00:02:44.470 --> 00:02:45.930
I agree.

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:50.810
Even we don't fully understand the
super-science on board this ship.

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:54.980
They may learn how to use it, but
they could never duplicate it.

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:57.280
But there's no reason to...

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:59.950
I can't stand this much longer!

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:04.530
How much longer are they going to
keep us cooped in this small space.

00:03:04.530 --> 00:03:07.790
There's no one to show
off my new suit to!

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:10.420
They all look the same to me.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:14.130
That's because you've got
no fashion sense!

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:16.000
There's a subtle difference.

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:19.550
It's more important to me whether I
can stay on board this ship or not.

00:03:19.550 --> 00:03:23.220
Are you kidding?! The earlier I can
get out, the happier I'll be!

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:28.350
But the scientific technology they
have is out of this world.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:32.810
I'd like to learn diving mechanics,
and apply it to the Gratan.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.650
Are you crazy?! They're not going to
teach you anything that easily.

00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.570
Maybe not.

00:03:38.570 --> 00:03:42.820
On the other hand, any decision we
make depends on our Senorita.

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.320
That's true.

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.540
Perfect...

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:57.550
"Senorita Grandis, you're
looking lovely today!"

00:03:57.550 --> 00:04:01.800
My! How nice of you to say so,
Captain Nemo! You flatter me!

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:05.600
"No, no! I never use flattery."

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.060
My! Then...

00:04:08.060 --> 00:04:09.770
Just dreaming!

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:16.190
I hereby confirm that Grandis,
Sanson and Hanson

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.730
will be taken on as apprentice crewmembers.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.690
Are you dissatisfied, Electra?

00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.650
No, it's just...

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:26.660
Can we really trust those three?

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.620
Especially Senorita Grandis.

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.290
What's suspicious about her?

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:34.830
Nothing.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.540
Nothing, really.

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:42.420
Apprentice crewmembers?!

00:04:42.670 --> 00:04:46.970
That's right. As of today, you three
will work under my command.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:50.010
This is kind of sudden, isn't it?

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.350
All right!

00:04:53.980 --> 00:04:56.310
Who's responsible for this?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:04.740
Dear God, thank you for listening
to my request!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.700
Oh, Captain Nemo...

00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:13.700
Miss Electra, I want to learn
about this ship!

00:05:15.120 --> 00:05:18.130
The science on board this
ship is superb.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.250
You're doing things no one
has ever done before.

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:26.430
I want to learn about your science,
and apply it for the good of man!

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:27.180
Good for you!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:35.180
I understand, Jean. But I cannot allow
you to wander the ship alone.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.820
Instead, you can read all the
books I have in my room.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:42.650
Thank you, Miss Electra!

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:47.820
Miss Electra, what should I do?

00:05:48.070 --> 00:05:51.370
You are to be treated as a guest,

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:55.500
but you will be expected to follow
all the rules just like Jean.

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.830
No, I want to be given
something to do too.

00:05:58.210 --> 00:05:58.920
But...

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:03.550
I've always worked for my food.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:07.380
Good for you. No work,
no food, as they say.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:11.350
I see. Then, you can assist Miss
Grandis with her work.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:12.350
Yes, Ma'am.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:14.310
I want to work too.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:17.020
Well, I wonder what job Marie can do?

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:18.980
I can do anything.

00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:22.980
I see. All right, I'll think of something
for you to do also.

00:06:26.820 --> 00:06:29.660
My goodness! So, you want
to work too, King?

00:06:33.830 --> 00:06:37.040
Control board for job assignments, switch on.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:42.880
Now, this is the interior of the
Nautilus. We're here right now.

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:48.420
This is the hangar, the crew's quarters
and the main Engine room.

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:51.680
Say, I don't see any propeller.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.890
Yeah, none.

00:06:52.890 --> 00:06:57.480
That's correct. This ship uses a
water jet for propulsion.

00:06:57.730 --> 00:06:59.350
Water jet?

00:06:59.350 --> 00:07:00.440
What's that?

00:07:00.440 --> 00:07:04.900
Water jet propulsion takes in water
through the inlet ports,

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:07.900
ionizes it, and through magnetic
induction by a super conductor coil

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:11.820
converts it to plasma and ejects it to
the rear, causing forward propulsion.

00:07:11.820 --> 00:07:14.950
You ionize the water, and apply
magnetic induction?

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:18.160
That requires tremendous power.
What's the power source?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:20.540
It's not possible with an ordinary
boiler or battery power.

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:24.000
The power source is here,
in the heart of the ship.

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:26.840
What's the principle behind
the power, Sir?

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:30.050
Hey, don't call me "Sir".
I'm not that old, you know?

00:07:30.050 --> 00:07:32.130
And the power source for
creating the jet stream?

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:36.350
That comes from our super efficient
parti... oups.

00:07:36.350 --> 00:07:37.680
What did you say?

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:42.650
I'm sorry, but I'm not allowed
to talk about that.

00:07:42.650 --> 00:07:46.610
Anyway, with this engine, nothing can
beat us, not even the Garfish.

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:48.070
The Garfish?

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:51.400
You saw it didn't you?
Gargoyle's submarine?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:53.990
The Garfish...

00:07:54.370 --> 00:07:57.580
Now, a special visit to the bridge.

00:07:57.580 --> 00:08:00.750
This is not allowed during
battle maneuvers.

00:08:02.620 --> 00:08:05.210
Marie, is something the matter?

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:08.500
Marie wants to work.
I don't like studying.

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:12.720
But Marie, children's work is to study.

00:08:13.010 --> 00:08:16.260
Marie is not a child!
That's why I want to work.

00:08:16.260 --> 00:08:19.520
But studying and working
are the same.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:20.980
Then, I don't want to work.

00:08:20.980 --> 00:08:22.020
Well, then what shall we do?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.690
My, how bright you are!

00:08:27.150 --> 00:08:29.480
Shall we study together, King?

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:34.740
Ready? What is one plus one?

00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.700
That's right, it's two.

00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.330
You know how to add?
I can't believe it.

00:08:45.460 --> 00:08:47.290
Marie can add too!

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:51.010
I see! Then, let's go to
the next problem.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:52.130
What is three minus two?

00:08:53.670 --> 00:08:56.010
King, this time it's my turn to answer.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.850
What are you wearing?
You look like a peasant.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:06.350
But it was too big for me,
so I cut it a bit.

00:09:06.350 --> 00:09:10.940
If that's how you like it. Now,
shall we go to the kitchen?

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:14.610
What is this?

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:15.820
Cold storage.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:16.990
Cold storage?

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:19.160
Everything looks frozen inside.

00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:21.290
Where is the ice?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:26.290
We don't use ice for cooling.
We use electricity.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.670
Electricity?

00:09:27.670 --> 00:09:29.750
Is electricity something cold?

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:34.590
I'm only the cook. I don't know
about such difficult things.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:36.340
What about this range?

00:09:36.550 --> 00:09:37.930
That's electric too.

00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:42.930
The oven?

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.390
The juicer?

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.680
The whipper?

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.310
The dishwasher?

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.480
The oven,

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:53.030
the juicer, the whipper

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:54.490
and the dishwasher too!

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:59.070
This is amazing. Everything
is run by electricity.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.660
Electricity sure sounds like a
convenient thing to have.

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.370
But there are two things
electricity cannot do.

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.420
One is to use this cooking knife,

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:12.880
and the other is to find pleasure
in feeding other people.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:19.260
You cut yourself again?

00:10:19.840 --> 00:10:23.600
Geez, kids nowadays can't
even cut seaweed.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:29.690
You certainly are a problem child.
You'll run out of fingers soon.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:36.530
You don't have to use the knife
anymore. Take off that cover.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.440
Sure...

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:47.870
That's right. You did tell me you
couldn't look at fish or meat.

00:10:49.830 --> 00:10:51.630
Hello?

00:10:52.500 --> 00:10:53.960
No one's home.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.970
Today, I'll cook the meal by myself.

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:01.260
Children and the aged can go
sit in a corner, and rest!

00:11:03.220 --> 00:11:07.680
We seem to have fish every day.
The menu must get monotonous!

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:10.140
I don't see how you can
touch those fish!

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:13.610
What're you so scared about?
It's not going to bite you.

00:11:14.690 --> 00:11:16.570
But they're all dead bodies!

00:11:16.780 --> 00:11:20.030
Dead bodies? What do you mean?
It's food to eat!

00:11:20.280 --> 00:11:25.530
It's food for my beloved
Captain Nemo to partake!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:34.500
Oh, what a delicious smell.
Now for a dash of my love!

00:11:35.590 --> 00:11:36.750
Oh, my goodness!

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.090
Your dinner is served!

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:46.680
What is this?

00:11:47.930 --> 00:11:52.900
This dish is called Angler Fish a la
Love, Grandis style. Please enjoy it.

00:11:53.150 --> 00:11:57.190
We get only soup and water.
Why's that?

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:01.400
Quiet! You're still young!
That won't kill you!

00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.200
Please, while it's hot!

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.500
My cooking doesn't please you?

00:12:15.670 --> 00:12:17.130
It's not that.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:24.220
It's delicious!

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:27.430
I'm so glad!

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:30.850
It might not look so good,
but it tastes great.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:34.190
Let me have a bite.
Say, this really is good!

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:36.480
It is? Here, give me a bite.

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.070
Say, this is tasty.

00:12:38.070 --> 00:12:40.400
I must agree, this is delicious.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:53.540
King's astonishing, but Grandis also
amazed me with her cooking.

00:12:53.540 --> 00:12:57.580
They say you can't judge a
person by his looks, but...

00:12:58.090 --> 00:12:59.040
But what?

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.050
It's about Nadia.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:03.760
What about Nadia?

00:13:03.760 --> 00:13:07.680
Well, she can't seem to do
anything right,

00:13:07.680 --> 00:13:11.850
but I'm sure she'll get over it in time.

00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:14.180
I see.

00:13:15.060 --> 00:13:18.480
Up to now, there's been no one
to teach her about life.

00:13:19.440 --> 00:13:23.110
I didn't have anyone like that either.

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:34.620
In other words,

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:38.040
in view of the food situation
on board the Nautilus,

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:41.460
this is the menu that resulted, but...

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:46.680
I'm sure everyone will bear with me.
Do I hear any complaints?!

00:13:48.840 --> 00:13:51.600
Now, shall we eat?

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:54.600
Isn't it grand to eat the same
food as Captain Nemo?

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:55.770
But...

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:58.940
You eat fish, and we get potatoes?

00:13:58.940 --> 00:14:03.400
What's that? You two have
something to say?!

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:07.530
Oh no! We were just saying how good
the mashed potatoes were.

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:12.280
Did you say mashed potatoes?
That's white fish meat.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.330
My, what bad manners!

00:14:16.330 --> 00:14:16.960
I'm sorry.

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:19.420
Time to eat!

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.050
Doesn't it smell delicious?

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:27.050
Maybe it needs a little pepper.

00:14:28.550 --> 00:14:31.640
It's not just lacking pepper.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:32.050
Right.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:34.890
Sanson! Hanson! If you have
any complaints, tell me!

00:14:35.310 --> 00:14:38.190
Speak up like men! You've been saying
things under your breath.

00:14:38.190 --> 00:14:42.060
It's disgusting. What do you expect
after loafing on your jobs?!

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:53.580
He's fast!

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:54.620
King!

00:14:57.040 --> 00:14:58.210
Darn him!

00:15:10.380 --> 00:15:12.050
King, you...

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:16.220
Senorita?!

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:17.680
That cat!

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:19.230
He's a lion.

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:25.730
I'll get you for scratching
my beautiful skin!

00:15:25.730 --> 00:15:26.570
Senorita!

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.610
Miss Grandis!

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:30.320
King, where are you?!

00:15:32.870 --> 00:15:33.700
There you are!

00:15:35.450 --> 00:15:36.540
Missed him!

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.700
Senorita...

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:38.500
Senorita!

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:40.710
Miss Grandis!

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:49.550
How rude everyone is during dinner!

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.840
What a strange bunch.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:15:58.680
King! King! King!

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:00.230
Wait, Miss Grandis!

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:32.550
King! King! King! King!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:39.310
Static electricity? What can it be?

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:41.390
We're coming in!

00:16:41.980 --> 00:16:46.860
Miss Grandis, what is this? You're
not permitted on the bridge!

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:50.440
It doesn't matter!
This is an emergency!

00:16:50.440 --> 00:16:55.780
Regardless of the reason, rules
must be strictly observed!

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:59.740
What are you talking about?
All you think about are rules!

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:02.450
That's why you look older
than you are!

00:17:02.450 --> 00:17:03.580
What did you say?!

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:12.170
I wonder what's in that room?

00:17:12.170 --> 00:17:14.800
King! King! King!

00:17:14.800 --> 00:17:16.130
Miss Grandis!

00:17:28.610 --> 00:17:30.610
So, this is where you were!

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:34.150
I wonder what this is?

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:35.900
It's definitely not a generator.

00:17:36.320 --> 00:17:38.120
Is it some kind of an engine?

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.370
That's right.

00:17:39.830 --> 00:17:40.830
Captain Nemo!

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:43.370
This is the heart of our submarine.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.080
A room temperature, particle
annihilation engine.

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.080
A particle annihilation engine?

00:17:48.080 --> 00:17:49.130
That's right.

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.670
What kind of engine is that?

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.920
Hydrogen atoms and anti-hydrogen
atoms annihilate each other,

00:17:55.920 --> 00:18:00.350
changing ninety-four percent of
their mass into pure energy.

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:02.510
It is the only existing near
perpetual engine.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:04.220
It seems very complicated.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:06.850
It is beyond the science
of the 19th century,

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:11.440
and even the 20th century,
to duplicate this engine.

00:18:13.900 --> 00:18:17.360
Depending on the application,
it can take us to the stars.

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:19.990
To the stars?

00:18:19.990 --> 00:18:22.450
Incredible! It's a treasure of mankind!

00:18:23.830 --> 00:18:25.450
A treasure of mankind...

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:33.170
But if it is applied evilly, it can be
a weapon to destroy the world.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:38.380
This ship at present is
only a killing tool.

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:42.390
Jean, science is truly a
wonderful thing.

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:44.100
It makes the impossible possible.

00:18:44.510 --> 00:18:47.100
But science must also
bear responsibility

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:50.060
for all human crimes caused by
partaking of the tree of knowledge.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:52.860
You must never forget that!

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:55.730
Get out of my way!

00:18:55.730 --> 00:19:00.160
I can't do that! Entrance into the
engine room is prohibited!

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:02.030
Don't be so uptight!

00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.700
No, it's prohibited!

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.990
I'm just going in to look for King.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:09.580
Whatever the reason, I cannot
allow you to pass.

00:19:09.580 --> 00:19:11.210
You mean that?!

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:12.290
King!

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.750
Where were you? I was so worried!

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.800
You must never run away again!

00:19:19.010 --> 00:19:25.010
Nadia dear, be a good girl and give
me the Blue Water... I mean, King!

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:28.430
Never! It all started because
you pestered King.

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:30.270
Hand him over!

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:31.480
What's going on?!

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:33.440
Captain!

00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:35.820
What's all the ruckus about?

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:37.230
It's...

00:19:39.780 --> 00:19:43.660
I just wanted to play with King a little.

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:57.300
In this day of modern science, why
must we be doing such manual labor?

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:02.300
As long as we're on board this ship,
this looks like our destiny.

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:04.090
What are you grumbling about?!

00:20:04.640 --> 00:20:08.060
This happened, because you two
aren't worth your bread!

00:20:09.020 --> 00:20:13.060
But isn't his angry face wonderful too?

00:20:32.710 --> 00:20:36.920
Oh, this feels so good!
I'd like to kiss the sky!

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:40.260
It's been so long since
we last saw the sun.

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:49.850
I never knew the wind and sun
could be so wonderful.

00:20:49.850 --> 00:20:51.560
Captain Nemo!

00:20:54.060 --> 00:20:56.230
You seemed so absorbed
in your books,

00:20:56.230 --> 00:21:00.070
but I guess you find the skies more
enjoyable than strict science.

00:21:01.530 --> 00:21:04.400
This ship will sail on the ocean's
surface for twenty-four hours.

00:21:04.400 --> 00:21:09.490
You are free to come out on
deck any time you wish.

00:21:09.870 --> 00:21:11.370
Yes, Sir!

00:21:13.210 --> 00:21:16.540
Please wait, Captain Nemo!

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.720
Jean, what's wrong?

00:21:29.050 --> 00:21:31.520
The more I read, the more
I don't understand.

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:34.230
I see. Do you think I could help you?

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:38.190
Tell me, is this ship a tool for killing?

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.150
Captain Nemo told you that, didn't he?

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:48.490
Yes, when I was looking for King, and
wandered into the engine room.

00:21:49.320 --> 00:21:50.990
I'm sorry! I should have told you.

00:21:50.990 --> 00:21:54.960
It's all right. I'll excuse you for
being honest in telling me.

00:21:58.630 --> 00:22:00.750
Science must assume responsibility
for the crimes committed

00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:03.210
by those that partake of the
tree of knowledge.

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:03.920
Is that what he said?

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:06.380
What does he mean?

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:09.340
How can I explain?

00:22:09.340 --> 00:22:13.680
As long as mankind has both
good and evil in its heart,

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:16.890
it creates good science and bad,

00:22:16.890 --> 00:22:19.860
because it is man that applies science.

00:22:19.860 --> 00:22:24.860
When man finds a force larger than he
can use, it causes great misery.

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:28.320
Like this ship.

00:22:32.410 --> 00:22:34.910
When man finds a force larger
than he can use,

00:22:34.910 --> 00:22:38.870
it causes great misery. Like this ship.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:43.340
Jean, there will come a time
when you will understand.

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:45.170
Jean... Jean!

00:22:46.010 --> 00:22:47.970
Your thoughts seem so far away.

00:22:48.300 --> 00:22:50.090
I'm sorry.

00:22:50.090 --> 00:22:52.010
Is it something Captain Nemo
said to you?

00:22:54.390 --> 00:22:58.890
Tell me, is this ship a good
one or a bad one?

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:01.020
I'm sure it must be a good one,

00:23:01.650 --> 00:23:03.860
because Captain Nemo is a good man!

00:23:07.900 --> 00:23:08.820
I wonder...

00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:31.010
The sea at night seems so scary.

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:32.640
So dark, as if it wants to swallow you.

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:39.140
Men are such small creatures
compared to this ocean.

00:23:40.060 --> 00:23:43.270
So insignificant when compared
to the limitless universe.
